question:
You are preparing a quick DEI trend readout.

Using the non-intersectional representation table, print a small report for a single workforce and year showing the reported percentages for race groups. The report should:
Accept a workforce name and report year as inputs.
Retrieve the corresponding row (if present) and print each race percentage with a clear label.
Apply simple control flow: if the workforce or year is missing (NULL or empty after trimming), print an explanatory message and stop.
Include robust exception handling for (a) no matching row and (b) multiple matching rows.

Requirements:
Procedure Name: Anonymous Block.
Parameters: None.
Output: DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Missing input: workforce and report year are required.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Workforce: ' || lv_workforce);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Report Year: ' || lv_report_year);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Race Asian: ' || lv_race_asian);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Race Black: ' || lv_race_black);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Race Hispanic/Latinx: ' || lv_race_hispanic_latinx);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Race Native American: ' || lv_race_native_american);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Race White: ' || lv_race_white);
Exception Handling: WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No data found.'
WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN: 'Multiple rows returned.'
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'

reference_answer:
DECLARE
  -- Inputs (set these before running)
  lv_workforce   GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_REPRESENTATION.workforce%TYPE := 'Google';
  lv_report_year GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_REPRESENTATION.report_year%TYPE := '2023';

  -- Retrieved values
  lv_race_asian             GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_REPRESENTATION.race_asian%TYPE;
  lv_race_black             GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_REPRESENTATION.race_black%TYPE;
  lv_race_hispanic_latinx   GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_REPRESENTATION.race_hispanic_latinx%TYPE;
  lv_race_native_american   GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_REPRESENTATION.race_native_american%TYPE;
  lv_race_white             GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_REPRESENTATION.race_white%TYPE;
BEGIN
  -- Basic input validation
  IF TRIM(lv_workforce) IS NULL OR TRIM(lv_report_year) IS NULL THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Missing input: workforce and report year are required.');
    RETURN;
  END IF;

  -- Single-row fetch for the requested workforce/year
  SELECT r.race_asian,
         r.race_black,
         r.race_hispanic_latinx,
         r.race_native_american,
         r.race_white
    INTO lv_race_asian,
         lv_race_black,
         lv_race_hispanic_latinx,
         lv_race_native_american,
         lv_race_white
    FROM GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_REPRESENTATION r
   WHERE r.workforce = lv_workforce
     AND r.report_year = lv_report_year;

  -- Output report
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Workforce: ' || lv_workforce);
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Report Year: ' || lv_report_year);
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Race Asian: ' || lv_race_asian);
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Race Black: ' || lv_race_black);
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Race Hispanic/Latinx: ' || lv_race_hispanic_latinx);
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Race Native American: ' || lv_race_native_american);
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Race White: ' || lv_race_white);
EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
  WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
  WHEN OTHERS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
END;

