question:
As part of a lightweight sales review, generate a small report of up to 15 sales territories showing their SalesYTD and a performance label. If the territory’s SalesYTD is above the overall average SalesYTD across all territories, label it as ABOVE_AVG; otherwise label it as BELOW_OR_EQUAL_AVG. Print one line per territory, ordered by SalesYTD descending.

Make sure the script safely handles cases where there is no data (or the average can’t be computed).

Requirements:
Procedure Name: Anonymous Block
Parameters: None
Output: DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Territory: ' || rec.name || ' | SalesYTD: ' || rec.salesytd || ' | Perf: ' || lv_perf_label);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
Exception Handling: WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No data found.'
WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN: 'Multiple rows returned.'
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'

reference_answer:
DECLARE
  co_report_limit CONSTANT PLS_INTEGER := 15; -- Limit output for report readability

  lv_avg_salesytd ADVENTUREWORKS.SALESTERRITORY.salesytd%TYPE;
  lv_perf_label   VARCHAR2(20);
BEGIN
  -- Get the overall average SalesYTD; if there are no rows, raise NO_DATA_FOUND explicitly.
  SELECT AVG(st.salesytd)
    INTO lv_avg_salesytd
    FROM ADVENTUREWORKS.SALESTERRITORY st;

  IF lv_avg_salesytd IS NULL THEN
    RAISE NO_DATA_FOUND;
  END IF;

  -- Report up to 15 territories ordered by SalesYTD.
  FOR rec IN (
    SELECT st.name, st.salesytd
      FROM ADVENTUREWORKS.SALESTERRITORY st
     ORDER BY st.salesytd DESC
     FETCH FIRST co_report_limit ROWS ONLY
  ) LOOP
    IF rec.salesytd > lv_avg_salesytd THEN
      lv_perf_label := 'ABOVE_AVG';
    ELSE
      lv_perf_label := 'BELOW_OR_EQUAL_AVG';
    END IF;

    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Territory: ' || rec.name || ' | SalesYTD: ' || rec.salesytd || ' | Perf: ' || lv_perf_label);
  END LOOP;
EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
  WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
  WHEN OTHERS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
END;
/

