question:
Build a reusable PL/SQL procedure that produces a compact year-by-year attrition index report for a given workforce in Google's DEI data.

The procedure should:
 Validate the input year range (start year must be <= end year).
 For each year in the range, pull the non-intersectional attrition index values for the workforce and print a single formatted line.
 If a year has no data, print a clear message for that year and continue to the next year (do not fail the whole run).
 Limit the total number of printed year lines to keep output readable.

Requirements:
Procedure Name: dei_attrition_report
Parameters:
p_workforce IN GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_ATTRITION_INDEX.workforce%TYPE
p_start_year IN GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_ATTRITION_INDEX.report_year%TYPE
p_end_year IN GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_ATTRITION_INDEX.report_year%TYPE
Output:
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Attrition Index Report (Non-Intersectional)');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Workforce=' || p_workforce || ', Years ' || p_start_year || '-' || p_end_year);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Year ' || lv_year || ': Women(US)=' || lv_us_women || ', Men(US)=' || lv_us_men || ', Women(Global)=' || lv_global_women || ', Men(Global)=' || lv_global_men);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Year ' || lv_year || ': No data found.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Input error: start year must be <= end year.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
Exception Handling:
WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No data found.'
WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN: 'Multiple rows returned.'
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'

reference_answer:
CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE dei_attrition_report(
  p_workforce   IN GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_ATTRITION_INDEX.workforce%TYPE,
  p_start_year  IN GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_ATTRITION_INDEX.report_year%TYPE,
  p_end_year    IN GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_ATTRITION_INDEX.report_year%TYPE
) IS
  co_line_limit CONSTANT PLS_INTEGER := 15; -- Limit output for report readability

  lv_start_year_num NUMBER;
  lv_end_year_num   NUMBER;
  lv_year           GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_ATTRITION_INDEX.report_year%TYPE;

  lv_us_women       GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_ATTRITION_INDEX.gender_us_women%TYPE;
  lv_us_men         GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_ATTRITION_INDEX.gender_us_men%TYPE;
  lv_global_women   GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_ATTRITION_INDEX.gender_global_women%TYPE;
  lv_global_men     GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_ATTRITION_INDEX.gender_global_men%TYPE;

  lv_printed_lines  PLS_INTEGER := 0;
BEGIN
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Attrition Index Report (Non-Intersectional)');
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Workforce=' || p_workforce || ', Years ' || p_start_year || '-' || p_end_year);

  -- Convert year strings to numbers for range validation and looping.
  lv_start_year_num := TO_NUMBER(p_start_year);
  lv_end_year_num   := TO_NUMBER(p_end_year);

  IF lv_start_year_num > lv_end_year_num THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Input error: start year must be <= end year.');
    RETURN;
  END IF;

  FOR i IN lv_start_year_num .. lv_end_year_num LOOP
    EXIT WHEN lv_printed_lines >= co_line_limit;

    lv_year := TO_CHAR(i);

    BEGIN
      SELECT a.gender_us_women,
             a.gender_us_men,
             a.gender_global_women,
             a.gender_global_men
        INTO lv_us_women,
             lv_us_men,
             lv_global_women,
             lv_global_men
        FROM GOOGLE_DEI.DAR_NON_INTERSECTIONAL_ATTRITION_INDEX a
       WHERE a.workforce = p_workforce
         AND a.report_year = lv_year;

      DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(
        'Year ' || lv_year || ': Women(US)=' || lv_us_women ||
        ', Men(US)=' || lv_us_men ||
        ', Women(Global)=' || lv_global_women ||
        ', Men(Global)=' || lv_global_men
      );

    EXCEPTION
      WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
        -- Year is missing for this workforce: keep going.
        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Year ' || lv_year || ': No data found.');
      WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN
        -- Data quality issue: keep going.
        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
      WHEN OTHERS THEN
        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
    END;

    lv_printed_lines := lv_printed_lines + 1;
  END LOOP;

EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
  WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
  WHEN OTHERS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
END dei_attrition_report;
/

