question:
Operations wants a quick diagnostic report for a single bikeshare station, but with data-quality checks.

Write an anonymous PL/SQL block that takes a station name (hardcoded in the block as a variable), finds the matching station_id, and then prints a small report (max 15 rows) of the most recent status snapshots for that station. For each snapshot, also classify the station as:
 'FULL' when docks_available = 0
 'EMPTY' when bikes_available = 0
 'BALANCED' otherwise

Because the status table stores numbers as VARCHAR2, you must safely convert the bikes/docks values to numbers and handle bad data. If the station name is missing/blank, print a clear message and do not query. Make sure the block never throws an unhandled exception.

Requirements:
Procedure Name: Anonymous Block
Parameters: None
Output: DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Station Report for: ' || lv_station_name || ' (station_id=' || lv_station_id || ')');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No station name provided.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(TO_CHAR(rec.time, 'YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI') || ' | bikes=' || rec.bikes_available_num || ' | docks=' || rec.docks_available_num || ' | state=' || rec.station_state);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
Exception Handling: WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No data found.'
WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN: 'Multiple rows returned.'
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'

tests:
SET SERVEROUTPUT ON;
DECLARE
  co_report_limit CONSTANT PLS_INTEGER := 15;
  lv_station_name SAN_FRANCISCO.BIKESHARE_STATIONS.name%TYPE := 'San Francisco Caltrain (Townsend at 4th)';
  lv_station_id   SAN_FRANCISCO.BIKESHARE_STATIONS.station_id%TYPE;
  lv_clean_name   SAN_FRANCISCO.BIKESHARE_STATIONS.name%TYPE;
BEGIN
  lv_clean_name := TRIM(lv_station_name);
  IF lv_clean_name IS NULL THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No station name provided.');
    RETURN;
  END IF;
  SELECT s.station_id INTO lv_station_id FROM SAN_FRANCISCO.BIKESHARE_STATIONS s WHERE s.name = lv_clean_name;
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Station Report for: ' || lv_station_name || ' (station_id=' || lv_station_id || ')');
  FOR rec IN (
    WITH latest_status AS (
      SELECT st.time,
             CASE WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(st.bikes_available, '^\s*\d+\s*$') THEN TO_NUMBER(TRIM(st.bikes_available)) ELSE 0 END AS bikes_available_num,
             CASE WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(st.docks_available, '^\s*\d+\s*$') THEN TO_NUMBER(TRIM(st.docks_available)) ELSE 0 END AS docks_available_num,
             CASE
               WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(st.docks_available, '^\s*\d+\s*$') AND TO_NUMBER(TRIM(st.docks_available)) = 0 THEN 'FULL'
               WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(st.bikes_available, '^\s*\d+\s*$') AND TO_NUMBER(TRIM(st.bikes_available)) = 0 THEN 'EMPTY'
               ELSE 'BALANCED'
             END AS station_state
        FROM SAN_FRANCISCO.BIKESHARE_STATUS st
       WHERE st.station_id = lv_station_id
       ORDER BY st.time DESC
    )
    SELECT ls.time, ls.bikes_available_num, ls.docks_available_num, ls.station_state
      FROM latest_status ls
     WHERE ROWNUM <= co_report_limit
     ORDER BY ls.time DESC
  ) LOOP
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(TO_CHAR(rec.time, 'YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI') || ' | bikes=' || rec.bikes_available_num || ' | docks=' || rec.docks_available_num || ' | state=' || rec.station_state);
  END LOOP;
EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
  WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
  WHEN OTHERS THEN DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
END;
/

