question:
Your public-health analytics team wants a reusable PL/SQL routine that prints a compact “county maternal profile” report for a given year.

Build a stored procedure that:
 Accepts a year (DATE) and an optional county FIPS (VARCHAR2). If the county FIPS is NULL, use the most common county FIPS in the dataset for that year.
 Uses an explicit cursor to fetch up to 15 rows from COUNTY_NATALITY for that year (and county if provided), ordered by births descending.
 For each row, compute an integer births value from the BIRTHS text column. If the conversion fails (non-numeric), treat births as 0.
 Track and print a summary at the end: total births across printed rows, number of rows printed, and the maximum births value seen.
 Make sure NO_DATA_FOUND, TOO_MANY_ROWS, and any other errors are handled cleanly with user-friendly DBMS_OUTPUT messages.

Requirements:
Procedure Name: report_county_maternal_profile
Parameters:
p_year IN SDOH_CDC_WONDER_NATALITY.COUNTY_NATALITY.year%TYPE
p_county_fips IN SDOH_CDC_WONDER_NATALITY.COUNTY_NATALITY.county_of_residence_fips%TYPE
Output:
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('County Maternal Profile Report');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Year=' || TO_CHAR(p_year, 'YYYY') || ', CountyFIPS=' || NVL(p_county_fips, ''));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Resolved CountyFIPS=' || lv_county_fips);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(RPAD('-', 70, '-'));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(RPAD('County', 30) || RPAD('FIPS', 12) || LPAD('Births', 10) || LPAD('AvgAge', 10));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(RPAD('-', 70, '-'));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(RPAD(lv_county_name, 30) || RPAD(lv_county_fips_row, 12) || LPAD(TO_CHAR(lv_births_num), 10) || LPAD(lv_age_disp, 10));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(RPAD('-', 70, '-'));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Rows printed=' || TO_CHAR(lv_rows_printed));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Total births=' || TO_CHAR(lv_total_births));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Max births=' || TO_CHAR(lv_max_births));
Exception Handling:
WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No data found.'
WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN: 'Multiple rows returned.'
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'

