question:
Build a reusable stored procedure that, for a given US state code, prints a small 'top agencies' report for home health agencies in that state.

The report should:
Validate the input state code (must be exactly 2 characters).
For that state, compute a numeric Medicare payment amount for each agency from TOTAL_HHA_MEDICARE_PAYMENT_AMOUNT_NON_LUPA (the source is stored as text), treating non-numeric or missing values as 0.
Classify each agency's payment as HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW using simple thresholds.
Print up to 15 agencies, ordered by payment descending, showing provider id, agency name, city, and the computed payment and classification.

Make sure the procedure never raises an unhandled error; print friendly messages for bad inputs or unexpected issues.

Requirements:
Procedure Name: report_hha_payments_by_state
Parameters:
p_state IN CMS_MEDICARE.HOME_HEALTH_AGENCIES.state%TYPE
Output:
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Top Home Health Agencies by Medicare Payment (Non-LUPA)');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('State: ' || p_state);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('PROVIDER_ID | AGENCY_NAME | CITY | PAYMENT | CATEGORY');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(rec.provider_id || ' | ' || rec.agency_name || ' | ' || rec.city || ' | ' || TO_CHAR(rec.payment_amt) || ' | ' || rec.category);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Invalid input: state code must be exactly 2 characters.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
Exception Handling:
WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No data found.'
WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN: 'Multiple rows returned.'
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'

reference_answer:
CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE report_hha_payments_by_state(
  p_state IN CMS_MEDICARE.HOME_HEALTH_AGENCIES.state%TYPE
) IS
  co_report_limit CONSTANT PLS_INTEGER := 15; -- Limit output for report readability
  lv_state        CMS_MEDICARE.HOME_HEALTH_AGENCIES.state%TYPE;
  v_count         PLS_INTEGER := 0;
BEGIN
  -- Validate input (basic data quality guard)
  IF p_state IS NULL OR LENGTH(TRIM(p_state)) <> 2 THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Invalid input: state code must be exactly 2 characters.');
    RETURN;
  END IF;

  lv_state := UPPER(TRIM(p_state));

  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Top Home Health Agencies by Medicare Payment (Non-LUPA)');
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('State: ' || lv_state);
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('PROVIDER_ID | AGENCY_NAME | CITY | PAYMENT | CATEGORY');

  -- Implicit cursor FOR loop (no explicit cursor declarations)
  FOR rec IN (
    SELECT *
    FROM (
      SELECT hha.provider_id,
             hha.agency_name,
             hha.city,
             CASE
               -- Treat non-numeric / missing as 0
               WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(TRIM(hha.total_hha_medicare_payment_amount_non_lupa), '^[-+]?[0-9]*\.?[0-9]+$')
                 THEN TO_NUMBER(TRIM(hha.total_hha_medicare_payment_amount_non_lupa))
               ELSE 0
             END AS payment_amt,
             CASE
               WHEN (CASE
                       WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(TRIM(hha.total_hha_medicare_payment_amount_non_lupa), '^[-+]?[0-9]*\.?[0-9]+$')
                         THEN TO_NUMBER(TRIM(hha.total_hha_medicare_payment_amount_non_lupa))
                       ELSE 0
                     END) >= 1000000 THEN 'HIGH'
               WHEN (CASE
                       WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(TRIM(hha.total_hha_medicare_payment_amount_non_lupa), '^[-+]?[0-9]*\.?[0-9]+$')
                         THEN TO_NUMBER(TRIM(hha.total_hha_medicare_payment_amount_non_lupa))
                       ELSE 0
                     END) >= 250000 THEN 'MEDIUM'
               ELSE 'LOW'
             END AS category
        FROM CMS_MEDICARE.HOME_HEALTH_AGENCIES hha
       WHERE hha.state = lv_state
       ORDER BY payment_amt DESC, hha.provider_id
    )
    WHERE ROWNUM <= co_report_limit
  ) LOOP
    v_count := v_count + 1;
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(
      rec.provider_id || ' | ' || rec.agency_name || ' | ' || rec.city || ' | ' || TO_CHAR(rec.payment_amt) || ' | ' || rec.category
    );
  END LOOP;

  IF v_count = 0 THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
  END IF;

EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
  WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
  WHEN OTHERS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
END report_hha_payments_by_state;
/

question:
As part of a compliance review, produce a small “Top Aliens” report for a given country.

Use a cursor to iterate through up to 15 aliens in that country (sorted by age descending, then last name/first name), and print one line per alien with their name, email, age, current location, and occupation. While iterating, also keep running totals of how many are marked aggressive vs non-aggressive.

After the loop, print a summary line with the totals and then print the most common favorite food for that country (if there is no favorite food data available, show a clear message instead).

Make sure the block handles bad inputs and runtime issues gracefully and never throws an unhandled exception.

Requirements:
Procedure Name: Anonymous Block
Parameters: None
Output: DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Top Aliens report for country = ' || lv_country);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Name=' || rec.first_name || ' ' || rec.last_name || ' | Email=' || rec.email || ' | Age=' || TO_CHAR(rec.age) || ' | Location=' || rec.current_location || ' | Occupation=' || rec.occupation || ' | Aggressive=' || CASE WHEN rec.aggressive = 1 THEN 'Y' ELSE 'N' END);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Summary: aggressive=' || TO_CHAR(lv_aggressive_cnt) || ', non_aggressive=' || TO_CHAR(lv_non_aggressive_cnt));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Most common favorite food: ' || lv_top_food);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No favorite food data found for this country.');
Exception Handling: WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No data found.'
WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN: 'Multiple rows returned.'
WHEN VALUE_ERROR THEN: 'Invalid input value.'
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'

reference_answer:
DECLARE
  co_report_limit CONSTANT PLS_INTEGER := 15; -- Limit output for report readability

  lv_country CITY_LEGISLATION.ALIEN_DATA.country%TYPE := 'USA';

  lv_aggressive_cnt     PLS_INTEGER := 0;
  lv_non_aggressive_cnt PLS_INTEGER := 0;

  lv_food_rows   PLS_INTEGER := 0;
  lv_top_food    CITY_LEGISLATION.ALIEN_DATA.favorite_food%TYPE;

  CURSOR cur_aliens(p_country CITY_LEGISLATION.ALIEN_DATA.country%TYPE) IS
    SELECT ad.first_name,
           ad.last_name,
           ad.email,
           ad.age,
           ad.current_location,
           ad.occupation,
           ad.aggressive
      FROM CITY_LEGISLATION.ALIEN_DATA ad
     WHERE ad.country = p_country
     ORDER BY ad.age DESC, ad.last_name, ad.first_name;
BEGIN
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Top Aliens report for country = ' || lv_country);

  -- Iterate via an explicit (named) cursor and cap output using the cursor attribute.
  FOR rec IN cur_aliens(lv_country) LOOP
    EXIT WHEN cur_aliens%ROWCOUNT > co_report_limit;

    IF rec.aggressive = 1 THEN
      lv_aggressive_cnt := lv_aggressive_cnt + 1;
    ELSE
      lv_non_aggressive_cnt := lv_non_aggressive_cnt + 1;
    END IF;

    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(
      'Name=' || rec.first_name || ' ' || rec.last_name ||
      ' | Email=' || rec.email ||
      ' | Age=' || TO_CHAR(rec.age) ||
      ' | Location=' || rec.current_location ||
      ' | Occupation=' || rec.occupation ||
      ' | Aggressive=' || CASE WHEN rec.aggressive = 1 THEN 'Y' ELSE 'N' END
    );
  END LOOP;

  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(
    'Summary: aggressive=' || TO_CHAR(lv_aggressive_cnt) ||
    ', non_aggressive=' || TO_CHAR(lv_non_aggressive_cnt)
  );

  -- Most common favorite food for the country.
  -- Use a row-limited subquery to keep the SELECT deterministic and safe.
  SELECT sub.favorite_food,
         sub.cnt
    INTO lv_top_food,
         lv_food_rows
    FROM (
          SELECT ad.favorite_food,
                 COUNT(*) AS cnt
            FROM CITY_LEGISLATION.ALIEN_DATA ad
           WHERE ad.country = lv_country
             AND ad.favorite_food IS NOT NULL
           GROUP BY ad.favorite_food
           ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC, ad.favorite_food
         ) sub
   WHERE ROWNUM = 1;

  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Most common favorite food: ' || lv_top_food);

EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
    -- Covers both: no aliens in the country, or no favorite food rows for the country.
    IF lv_food_rows = 0 THEN
      DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No favorite food data found for this country.');
    ELSE
      DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
    END IF;
  WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
  WHEN VALUE_ERROR THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Invalid input value.');
  WHEN OTHERS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
END;
/

