question:
Build a reusable routine that produces a small “county natality snapshot” report for a given year and optional county name filter. The report should scan the county_natality dataset, print up to 15 counties with the highest number of births, and also print a few quality indicators (how many rows had non-numeric births, min/max births among parsable rows, and the average mother age among parsable rows). Since the source columns are stored as strings, the routine must safely handle non-numeric values and continue processing. If the county filter is provided, only include counties whose name contains the filter (case-insensitive).

Requirements:
Procedure Name: natality_reporting.print_county_snapshot
Parameters:
p_year IN SDOH_CDC_WONDER_NATALITY.COUNTY_NATALITY.year%TYPE
p_county_filter IN SDOH_CDC_WONDER_NATALITY.COUNTY_NATALITY.county_of_residence%TYPE
Output:
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('County natality snapshot');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Year: ' || TO_CHAR(p_year, 'YYYY'));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('County filter: ' || NVL(p_county_filter, ''));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Top counties by births (up to ' || co_report_limit || ' rows)');
